IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`
IMPORT `roc4-order-19-div-1`
IMPORT `roc4-order-19-div-2`
IMPORT `roc4-order-19-div-3`
IMPORT `roc4-order-19-div-4`
IMPORT `roc4-order-19-duties`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), Order 19: tests of the regulative rules (roc4-order-19-duties.l4) and of their decision-function twins.
-- The text is a converter rendering of Singapore Statutes Online, not the official text.
-- A regulative rule cannot be asserted on the main binary (NOTES.md, "What the main binary does not accept"), so each #TRACE has its expected outcome written beside it from the text,
-- and the outcome is checked by reading the trace (NOTES.md records that it was read on 1.6.109 and 1.6.108 and what each printed).
-- The assertions test the twins, with the same facts: a clock that starts at day 0 and a last day that is that many days later.
-- Example: a judgment dated 27 January 2026; fourteen days after it, counted under Order 3, rule 3, is 10 February 2026.

-- ===== Rule 8(3): MAY apply within 14 days =====
-- Expected from rule 8(3): the application on day 10 is within the 14 days: FULFILLED.  An application on day 15, after the 14 days, finds the permission lapsed: FULFILLED (a permission unused is not a breach; the rule has no LEST, so both dialects read it alike).
#TRACE `o 19 r 8(3) the absent party may file and serve an application to restore the appeal within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 8(3) the absent party` DOES `o 19 r 8(3) file and serve an application to restore the appeal` AT 10
#TRACE `o 19 r 8(3) the absent party may file and serve an application to restore the appeal within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 8(3) the absent party` DOES `o 19 r 8(3) file and serve an application to restore the appeal` AT 15
-- Twin: filed and served on the last day, a day late.  (The dismissal was on 27 January 2026; the last day is 10 February 2026.)
#ASSERT `o 19 r 8(3) the application to restore the appeal is filed and served in time` (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 8(3) the application to restore the appeal is filed and served in time` (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 11 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ===== Rule 14(1): MUST file and serve the notice of appeal within 14 days =====
-- Expected from rule 14(1): on day 14, FULFILLED; on day 15, a day after the 14 days, BREACH.
#TRACE `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant must file and serve the notice of appeal within 14 days after the date of the judgment` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 14(1) file and serve the notice of appeal` AT 14
#TRACE `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant must file and serve the notice of appeal within 14 days after the date of the judgment` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 14(1) file and serve the notice of appeal` AT 15
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(1) the notice of appeal is filed and served as required` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(1) the notice of appeal is filed and served as required` TRUE TRUE (Date 11 2 2026) (Date 11 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ===== Rule 17(4), (8), (10): the chain of documents =====
-- The argument after the rule's name says whether there is a Reply, a second core bundle or a second bundle of authorities to file (paragraph (10) names only items "(if any)" and "(if necessary)").
-- Expected from rule 17: the appellant on day 28 (the Registry informed the parties on day 0); the respondent 28 days after the appellant served, day 56; the Reply 14 days after that, day 70: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `o 19 r 17(4) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 28 days and the respondent and the appellant must follow` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 17(4) file and serve the record of appeal, the appellant's Case, the appellant's core bundle of documents and the appellant's bundle of authorities` AT 28
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 17(8) file and serve the respondent's Case, the respondent's core bundle of documents (if necessary) and the respondent's bundle of authorities` AT 56
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 17(10) file and serve the appellant's Reply (if any), the second core bundle (if necessary) and the appellant's second bundle of authorities (if any)` AT 70
-- Expected: the same, with nothing to file under paragraph (10): FULFILLED after the respondent's Case on day 56, with no third step.
#TRACE `o 19 r 17(4) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 28 days and the respondent and the appellant must follow` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 17(4) file and serve the record of appeal, the appellant's Case, the appellant's core bundle of documents and the appellant's bundle of authorities` AT 28
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 17(8) file and serve the respondent's Case, the respondent's core bundle of documents (if necessary) and the respondent's bundle of authorities` AT 56
-- Expected: the Reply on day 71, a day after the 14 days: BREACH by the appellant (the text names no consequence).
#TRACE `o 19 r 17(4) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 28 days and the respondent and the appellant must follow` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 17(4) file and serve the record of appeal, the appellant's Case, the appellant's core bundle of documents and the appellant's bundle of authorities` AT 28
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 17(8) file and serve the respondent's Case, the respondent's core bundle of documents (if necessary) and the respondent's bundle of authorities` AT 56
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 17(10) file and serve the appellant's Reply (if any), the second core bundle (if necessary) and the appellant's second bundle of authorities (if any)` AT 71
-- Expected: the appellant on day 29, a day late: BREACH by the appellant (the appeal is deemed withdrawn, paragraph (5)).
#TRACE `o 19 r 17(4) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 28 days and the respondent and the appellant must follow` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 17(4) file and serve the record of appeal, the appellant's Case, the appellant's core bundle of documents and the appellant's bundle of authorities` AT 29
-- Expected: the respondent on day 57, a day late (the appellant served on day 28): BREACH by the respondent (barred, paragraph (9)).
#TRACE `o 19 r 17(4) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 28 days and the respondent and the appellant must follow` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 17(4) file and serve the record of appeal, the appellant's Case, the appellant's core bundle of documents and the appellant's bundle of authorities` AT 28
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 17(8) file and serve the respondent's Case, the respondent's core bundle of documents (if necessary) and the respondent's bundle of authorities` AT 57
-- Twins, with the Registry's notice on 2 March 2026 (28 days later is 30 March 2026), the appellant's service on 30 March 2026 (28 days later is 27 April 2026).
#ASSERT `o 19 r 17(4) the appellant's document is filed and served in time` `o 19 r 17(4)(b) the appellant's Case` TRUE (Date 30 3 2026) (Date 30 3 2026) (Date 30 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 17(4) the appellant's document is filed and served in time` `o 19 r 17(4)(b) the appellant's Case` TRUE (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 30 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 17(5) the appeal is deemed withdrawn` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent's document is filed and served in time` `o 19 r 17(8)(a) the respondent's Case` TRUE (Date 27 4 2026) (Date 27 4 2026) (Date 27 4 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent's document is filed and served in time` `o 19 r 17(8)(a) the respondent's Case` TRUE (Date 28 4 2026) (Date 28 4 2026) (Date 27 4 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent is barred from making submissions at the hearing of the appeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 17(10) the appellant's reply document is filed and served in time` `o 19 r 17(10)(a) the appellant's Reply` TRUE (Date 11 5 2026) (Date 11 5 2026) (Date 11 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 17(10) the appellant's reply document is filed and served in time` `o 19 r 17(10)(a) the appellant's Reply` TRUE (Date 12 5 2026) (Date 12 5 2026) (Date 11 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ===== Rule 22: MUST file a certified copy with the Registrar of the State Courts, no time limit =====
-- Expected from rule 22: done on day 5: FULFILLED.  The text gives no time limit, so no day makes it late.
#TRACE `o 19 r 22 the appellant must file a certified copy of the General Division's judgment or order with the Registrar of the State Courts` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 22 file a certified copy of the General Division's judgment or order with the Registrar of the State Courts` AT 5
#TRACE `o 19 r 22 the appellant must file a certified copy of the General Division's judgment or order with the Registrar of the State Courts` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 22 file a certified copy of the General Division's judgment or order with the Registrar of the State Courts` AT 400
#ASSERT `o 19 r 22 the appellant has notified the Registrar of the State Courts of the General Division's judgment or order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 22 the appellant has notified the Registrar of the State Courts of the General Division's judgment or order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ===== Rule 25(1): MUST file and serve the notice of appeal within 28 days =====
-- Expected from rule 25(1): day 28 FULFILLED; day 29 BREACH.
#TRACE `o 19 r 25(1) the appellant must file and serve the notice of appeal within 28 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 25(1) file and serve the notice of appeal to the appellate Court` AT 28
#TRACE `o 19 r 25(1) the appellant must file and serve the notice of appeal within 28 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 25(1) file and serve the notice of appeal to the appellate Court` AT 29
#ASSERT `o 19 r 25(1) the notice of appeal is filed and served as required` TRUE TRUE (Date 24 2 2026) (Date 24 2 2026) (Date 24 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 25(1) the notice of appeal is filed and served as required` TRUE TRUE (Date 25 2 2026) (Date 25 2 2026) (Date 24 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ===== Rule 41(2), (3): eight weeks, then 28 days =====
-- Expected from rule 41: the appellant on day 56 (8 weeks), the respondent 28 days after that, day 84: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `o 19 r 41(2) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 8 weeks and the respondent must follow within 28 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 41(2) file and serve the record of proceedings, the appellant's written submissions and the appellant's bundle of authorities` AT 56
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 41(3) file and serve the respondent's written submissions and the respondent's bundle of authorities` AT 84
-- Expected: the appellant on day 57, a day late: BREACH by the appellant.
#TRACE `o 19 r 41(2) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 8 weeks and the respondent must follow within 28 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 41(2) file and serve the record of proceedings, the appellant's written submissions and the appellant's bundle of authorities` AT 57
-- Expected: the respondent on day 85, a day late: BREACH by the respondent.
#TRACE `o 19 r 41(2) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 8 weeks and the respondent must follow within 28 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 41(2) file and serve the record of proceedings, the appellant's written submissions and the appellant's bundle of authorities` AT 56
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 41(3) file and serve the respondent's written submissions and the respondent's bundle of authorities` AT 85
-- Twins, with the Registry's notice on 2 March 2026 (8 weeks later is 27 April 2026) and the appellant's service on 27 April 2026 (28 days later is 25 May 2026).
#ASSERT `o 19 r 41(2) the appellant's document is filed and served in time` `o 19 r 41(2)(a) the record of proceedings` (Date 27 4 2026) (Date 27 4 2026) (Date 27 4 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 41(2) the appellant's document is filed and served in time` `o 19 r 41(2)(a) the record of proceedings` (Date 28 4 2026) (Date 28 4 2026) (Date 27 4 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 41(3) the respondent's document is filed and served in time` `o 19 r 41(3)(a) the respondent's written submissions` (Date 25 5 2026) (Date 25 5 2026) (Date 25 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 41(3) the respondent's document is filed and served in time` `o 19 r 41(3)(a) the respondent's written submissions` (Date 26 5 2026) (Date 26 5 2026) (Date 25 5 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE


-- ===== Further timed duties: 14 days each =====
-- Expected for each of the rules below: the act on day 14 is in time (FULFILLED); the act on day 15 is a day late (BREACH by that party).
-- Rule 15(1): 14 days after the date of the judgment.
#TRACE `o 19 r 15(1) the party must apply to the lower Court for permission and serve the application within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 15(1) the party who needs permission to appeal` DOES `o 19 r 15(1) apply to the lower Court for permission to appeal and serve the application` AT 14
#TRACE `o 19 r 15(1) the party must apply to the lower Court for permission and serve the application within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 15(1) the party who needs permission to appeal` DOES `o 19 r 15(1) apply to the lower Court for permission to appeal and serve the application` AT 15
-- Rule 15(3): 14 days after the decision granting permission.
#TRACE `o 19 r 15(3) the applicant must file and serve the notice of appeal within 14 days after permission is granted` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 15(1) the party who needs permission to appeal` DOES `o 19 r 15(3) file and serve the notice of appeal after permission is granted` AT 14
#TRACE `o 19 r 15(3) the applicant must file and serve the notice of appeal within 14 days after permission is granted` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 15(1) the party who needs permission to appeal` DOES `o 19 r 15(3) file and serve the notice of appeal after permission is granted` AT 15
-- Rule 26(1): 14 days after the date of the lower Court's decision.
#TRACE `o 19 r 26(1) the party must apply for permission and file and serve the application within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 15(1) the party who needs permission to appeal` DOES `o 19 r 26(1) apply to the appellate Court for permission to appeal and file and serve the application and the documents mentioned in paragraph (7)` AT 14
#TRACE `o 19 r 26(1) the party must apply for permission and file and serve the application within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 15(1) the party who needs permission to appeal` DOES `o 19 r 26(1) apply to the appellate Court for permission to appeal and file and serve the application and the documents mentioned in paragraph (7)` AT 15
-- Rule 26(8): 14 days after the application and its documents are served on the party.
#TRACE `o 19 r 26(8) the party who opposes must file and serve written submissions within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 26(8) the party who opposes the application for permission` DOES `o 19 r 26(8) file and serve written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities in opposition` AT 14
#TRACE `o 19 r 26(8) the party who opposes must file and serve written submissions within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 26(8) the party who opposes the application for permission` DOES `o 19 r 26(8) file and serve written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities in opposition` AT 15
-- Rule 26(17): 14 days after the decision granting permission.
#TRACE `o 19 r 26(17) the applicant must file and serve the notice of appeal within 14 days after permission is granted` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 15(1) the party who needs permission to appeal` DOES `o 19 r 26(17) file and serve the notice of appeal after permission is granted` AT 14
#TRACE `o 19 r 26(17) the applicant must file and serve the notice of appeal within 14 days after permission is granted` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 15(1) the party who needs permission to appeal` DOES `o 19 r 26(17) file and serve the notice of appeal after permission is granted` AT 15
-- Rule 35(14): 14 days after service of the notice of the appeal on the applicant.
#TRACE `o 19 r 35(14) the applicant must file and serve the summons and the supporting affidavit within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 35(14) the applicant` DOES `o 19 r 35(14) file and serve the summons and the supporting affidavit` AT 14
#TRACE `o 19 r 35(14) the applicant must file and serve the summons and the supporting affidavit within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 35(14) the applicant` DOES `o 19 r 35(14) file and serve the summons and the supporting affidavit` AT 15
-- Rule 36: 14 days after the direction or order is made.
#TRACE `o 19 r 36 the applicant must file and serve the application for permission within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 36 the applicant for the permission` DOES `o 19 r 36 file and serve the application for permission` AT 14
#TRACE `o 19 r 36 the applicant must file and serve the application for permission within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 36 the applicant for the permission` DOES `o 19 r 36 file and serve the application for permission` AT 15

-- ===== Rule 30(4), (9), (11): the chain of documents, 8 weeks then 28 days then 14 days =====
-- The argument after the rule's name says whether there is a Reply, a second core bundle or a second bundle of authorities to file.
-- Expected: the appellant on day 56 (8 weeks), the respondent 28 days after the appellant served, day 84, the Reply 14 days after that, day 98: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `o 19 r 30(4) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 8 weeks and the respondent and the appellant must follow` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 30(4) file and serve the documents mentioned in paragraph (4) or, on an appeal from the Appellate Division, paragraph (5)` AT 56
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 30(9) file and serve the respondent's Case, the respondent's core bundle of documents (if necessary) and the respondent's bundle of authorities` AT 84
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 30(11) file and serve the appellant's Reply (if any), the second core bundle (if necessary) and the appellant's second bundle of authorities (if any)` AT 98
-- Expected: nothing to file under paragraph (11): FULFILLED after the respondent's Case on day 84.
#TRACE `o 19 r 30(4) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 8 weeks and the respondent and the appellant must follow` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 30(4) file and serve the documents mentioned in paragraph (4) or, on an appeal from the Appellate Division, paragraph (5)` AT 56
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 30(9) file and serve the respondent's Case, the respondent's core bundle of documents (if necessary) and the respondent's bundle of authorities` AT 84
-- Expected: the appellant on day 57, a day late: BREACH by the appellant (the appeal is deemed withdrawn, paragraph (6)).
#TRACE `o 19 r 30(4) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 8 weeks and the respondent and the appellant must follow` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 30(4) file and serve the documents mentioned in paragraph (4) or, on an appeal from the Appellate Division, paragraph (5)` AT 57
-- Expected: the respondent on day 85, a day late: BREACH by the respondent (barred, paragraph (10)).
#TRACE `o 19 r 30(4) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 8 weeks and the respondent and the appellant must follow` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 30(4) file and serve the documents mentioned in paragraph (4) or, on an appeal from the Appellate Division, paragraph (5)` AT 56
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 30(9) file and serve the respondent's Case, the respondent's core bundle of documents (if necessary) and the respondent's bundle of authorities` AT 85
-- Expected: the Reply on day 99, a day late: BREACH by the appellant (the text names no consequence).
#TRACE `o 19 r 30(4) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 8 weeks and the respondent and the appellant must follow` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 30(4) file and serve the documents mentioned in paragraph (4) or, on an appeal from the Appellate Division, paragraph (5)` AT 56
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 30(9) file and serve the respondent's Case, the respondent's core bundle of documents (if necessary) and the respondent's bundle of authorities` AT 84
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` DOES `o 19 r 30(11) file and serve the appellant's Reply (if any), the second core bundle (if necessary) and the appellant's second bundle of authorities (if any)` AT 99

-- ===== Rules 17(9), 18(3), 30(10), 31(3): the bars that name the respondent =====
-- Each rule takes two facts: whether the respondent failed to do the thing, and whether the Court has otherwise ordered.
-- Expected for each: bar holds (failed, no order) and the respondent makes the submissions: BREACH by the respondent.
-- Bar does not hold (did not fail, or the Court has otherwise ordered) and the respondent makes the submissions: FULFILLED (nothing forbidden).
-- o 19 r 17(9): failed, no order: bar holds.
#TRACE `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent shall not make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 17(9) make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` AT 5
-- o 19 r 17(9): did not fail: no bar.
#TRACE `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent shall not make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 17(9) make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` AT 5
-- o 19 r 17(9): failed but the Court has otherwise ordered: no bar.
#TRACE `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent shall not make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 17(9) make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` AT 5
-- o 19 r 18(3): failed, no order: bar holds.
#TRACE `o 19 r 18(3) the respondent shall not make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 18(3) make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` AT 5
-- o 19 r 18(3): did not fail: no bar.
#TRACE `o 19 r 18(3) the respondent shall not make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 18(3) make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` AT 5
-- o 19 r 18(3): failed but the Court has otherwise ordered: no bar.
#TRACE `o 19 r 18(3) the respondent shall not make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 18(3) make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` AT 5
-- o 19 r 30(10): failed, no order: bar holds.
#TRACE `o 19 r 30(10) the respondent shall not make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 17(9) make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` AT 5
-- o 19 r 30(10): did not fail: no bar.
#TRACE `o 19 r 30(10) the respondent shall not make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 17(9) make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` AT 5
-- o 19 r 30(10): failed but the Court has otherwise ordered: no bar.
#TRACE `o 19 r 30(10) the respondent shall not make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 17(9) make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` AT 5
-- o 19 r 31(3): failed, no order: bar holds.
#TRACE `o 19 r 31(3) the respondent shall not make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 18(3) make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` AT 5
-- o 19 r 31(3): did not fail: no bar.
#TRACE `o 19 r 31(3) the respondent shall not make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 18(3) make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` AT 5
-- o 19 r 31(3): failed but the Court has otherwise ordered: no bar.
#TRACE `o 19 r 31(3) the respondent shall not make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent` DOES `o 19 r 18(3) make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` AT 5
